<div class="page">
  <div class="header-logo">
    <div class="logo-graphic"></div>
    <div class="logo-text">
      <h1>LAKESHORE</h1>
      <h2>TECHNICAL COLLEGE</h2>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-title">Memorandum of Understanding &amp; Articulated Agreement between</h2>
  <h1 class="section-title" style="font-size: 16pt;">Lakeshore Technical College and University of Wisconsin Oshkosh Associate of Arts/Associate of Science</h1>

  <p class="paragraph">
    Lakeshore Technical College (LTC) and the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh (UWO) will cooperate in the delivery of <span data-field="agreement_type">{{ agreement_type }}</span>. This memorandum of understanding describes the intent, spirit, and commitment of both parties in collaboration.
  </p>

  <h3 class="section-title">Wisconsin Technical College System (WTCS) Mission and Purpose:</h3>
  <p class="paragraph">
    &ldquo;to provide a system of technical colleges which enables eligible persons to acquire the occupational skills training necessary for full participation in the work force; which stresses job training and retraining; which recognizes the rapidly changing educational needs of residents to keep current with the demands of the work place and through its course offerings and programs facilitates educational options for residents; which fosters economic development; which provides education through associate degree programs and other programs below the baccalaureate level; which functions cooperatively with other educational institutions and other governmental bodies; and which provides services to all members of the public.&rdquo; (Wisconsin Statute, Chapter 38.001)
  </p>

  <p class="paragraph">
    The additional purpose of the technical college system: &ldquo;Provide a collegiate transfer program.&rdquo; (Wisconsin Statute, Chapter 38.001(3)(b), 38.01(3).)
  </p>

  <h3 class="section-title">Lakeshore Technical College Mission and Vision:</h3>
  <p class="paragraph">
    Mission – Transform individuals to strengthen our communities through innovative and accessible learning.
  </p>
  <p class="paragraph">
    Vision – The community’s driver for individual, social, cultural, and economic vitality.
  </p>

  <h3 class="section-title">University of Wisconsin Oshkosh Mission, Vision and Values:</h3>
  <p class="paragraph">
    Mission
  </p>
  <p class="paragraph">
    The University of Wisconsin – Oshkosh provides a high-quality liberal education to all of its students in order to prepare them to become successful leaders in an increasingly diverse and global society. Our dedicated faculty and staff are committed to innovative teaching, research, economic development, entrepreneurship and community engagement to create a more sustainable future for Wisconsin and beyond. High quality academic programs in nursing, education, business, social sciences, natural sciences, humanities, fine and performing arts, engineering technology, information technology, health sciences and applied and liberal studies – all delivered in an innovative and inclusive learning environment – lead to degrees at the associate, baccalaureate, master’s and professional doctorate levels.
  </p>
  <p class="paragraph">
    Vision:
  </p>
  <p class="paragraph">
    The University of Wisconsin Oshkosh will be a research-enhanced comprehensive university built upon the ideals of a liberal education, inclusive excellence and shared governance that reinforces a nationally recognized emphasis on sustainability.
  </p>
  <p class="paragraph">
    Values:
  </p>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="values[0]">{{ values[0] }}</span></li>
    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="values[1]">{{ values[1] }}</span></li>
    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="values[2]">{{ values[2] }}</span></li>
    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="values[3]">{{ values[3] }}</span></li>
  </ul>

  <p class="paragraph">
    <span data-field="contact_info">{{ contact_info }}</span>
  </p>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-logo">
    <div class="logo-graphic"></div>
    <div class="logo-text">
      <h1>LAKESHORE</h1>
      <h2>TECHNICAL COLLEGE</h2>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="section-title">Community Partnerships</h2>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="partnership_area[0]">{{ partnership_area[0] }}</span></li>
    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="partnership_area[1]">{{ partnership_area[1] }}</span></li>
    <li class="list-item"><span data-field="partnership_area[2]">{{ partnership_area[2] }}</span></li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="section-title">Overall Objectives</h2>
  <p class="paragraph">
    The General Studies Transfer – Associate of Arts/Associate of Science degrees are designed to prepare students to enter Baccalaureate programs with a junior status at the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh. Upon completion, students will have met the general education requirements of the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh, with up to 60 credits, based on individual course selection, eligible for guaranteed admission and transfer. Elective options will allow students to select courses that appeal to their career plans. The curriculum proposed will provide sufficient options for enrollees to complete the associate degree requirements in two years and the bachelor’s degree requirements in four years.
  </p>
  <p class="paragraph">
    Lakeshore Technical College (LTC) and the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh (UWO) have developed a guaranteed transfer agreement (see Appendix A). LTC and UWO agree to commit to a partnership under this terms of memorandum of understanding (MOU) and all its incorporated attachments.
  </p>

  <h3 class="section-title">Demonstration of Need</h3>
  <p class="paragraph">
    LTC has reviewed courses that are part of current Wisconsin Technical College System (WTCS) university transfer degrees to align in title and number. LTC classes will be available through in-person, online, virtual (online synchronous), or a combination of delivery modes, with some exceptions. Students will need to complete a minimum of 25% of the degree, or 16 credits, at LTC; the degree is awarded by LTC.
  </p>

  <h4 style="font-size: 12pt; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 20px;">Supporting Documentation:</h4>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li class="list-item">Lakeshore Technical College and UW Oshkosh seek to close the attainment gap by expanding and maximizing access to postsecondary education in the LTC District. The Lumina Foundation, A Stronger Nation’s Report 2019, provides data regarding the attainment rate in Wisconsin and by county. According to the Lumina Foundation, “Wisconsin’s attainment rate is 54.7 percent, and the state is working toward its attainment goal of 60 percent by 2027.” The LTC district average is 46.5% (Calumet – 48.4%, Manitowoc – 35.9%, Ozaukee – 62.0%; Sheboygan – 39.5%).</li>
    <li class="list-item">Lakeshore Technical College and the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh seek to better serve residents who already are seeking a transfer degree.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Lakeshore Technical College and the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh hope to further expand baccalaureate partnerships within the region. According to research completed by the Jack Kent Cooke Foundation, in the report titled, Persistence: The Success of Students who Transfer from Community Colleges to Selective Four-Year Institutions, it was found “that community college transfer students have equal to higher graduation rates than students enrolling from high school or transferring from other four-year institutions.”</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-logo">
    <div class="logo-graphic"></div>
    <div class="logo-text">
      <h1>LAKESHORE</h1>
      <h2>TECHNICAL COLLEGE</h2>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3 class="section-title">Guiding Principles</h3>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li class="list-item">Both institutions will contribute resources and expertise toward the common goal of providing the opportunity for students to earn a General Studies Transfer – Associate of Arts/Associate of Science degree transfer toward a baccalaureate degree.</li>
    <li class="list-item">The institutions will create a consortium agreement for enrolled students to earn a General Studies Transfer – Associate of Arts or Associate of Science Degree, conferred by Lakeshore Technical College, as approved by the WTCS Board and the UW System Board of Regents.</li>
    <li class="list-item">The institutions will work collaboratively to transcript the courses and review and update the information annually.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Each institution will maintain their own college accreditation and LTC will maintain all documentation on program direction, program planning and the encompassing agreements.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Each institution will participate in jointly marketing the new program collaboration, including noting it in appropriate institutional publications and web content.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Collaborative promotional materials for the General Studies Transfer – Associate of Arts/Associate of Science degrees will be created.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Subject to FERPA and other restrictions, data on enrollment, retention, pre- and post-transfer, completion, and graduation will be shared annually between the partnering institutions.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Please see Appendix C: Assessment.</li>
    <li class="list-item">LTC and UWO will meet regularly to assure learning needs are met with the agreement.</li>
    <li class="list-item">LTC and UWO faculty may participate in an Advisory Committee to understand employer needs.</li>
    <li class="list-item">This agreement is subject to review if either LTC or UWO undergoes curriculum revision OR within five years of the origination of this agreement, whichever occurs earlier.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 class="section-title">Partner Roles and Responsibilities</h3>
  <p class="paragraph">
    Lakeshore Technical College will:
  </p>
  <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 20px;">
    <li class="list-item">Ensure all collaborative program documentation is accurate, up-to-date, and appropriate approvals have been obtained from the Wisconsin Technical College System Office.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Provide program direction for the entire curriculum, including a plan for program marketing.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Assess Credit for Prior Learning based on WTCS standards.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Assign a Dean to oversee program oversight and supervision.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Award financial aid to students within the Associate Degree programs.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Hire and supervise instructors for courses offered as part of the degree program.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Confer the General Studies Transfer – Associate of Arts/Associate of Science degrees.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Process student applications and collect applicable fees.</li>
    <li class="list-item">Provide advising and support services.</li>
    <li class="list-item">LTC will provide academic advising to assist new students enrolling in this program.</li>
  </ul>

  <p class="paragraph">
    <span data-field="signature_text">{{ signature_text }}</span>
  </p>
</div>

