  <h3 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 40px;">APPENDIX C</h3>
  <h2 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 10px;">Assessment</h2>
  <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The General Studies Transfer – Associate of Arts and Associate of Science partnership between Lakeshore Technical College and the University of Wisconsin Oshkosh will use both quantitative and qualitative data when assessing student learning and overall program viability. The partners will address the program and course learning outcomes in their cooperative development of the assessment plan.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Direct measures and indirect measures of student success will be used as assessment measures. Indirect measures of student learning could be gathered from graduate surveys, alumni surveys, or focus group discussions.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The Program Outcomes for the General Studies Transfer – Associate of Arts and Associate of Science partnership are based on the LTC Employability Skills as shown below in Chart 1 Program Outcomes.</p>
    <h4 style="text-align: center; margin-top: 30px;">Chart 1: General Studies Transfer – AA/AS Agreement Program Outcomes</h4>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th style="width: 50%;">Program Outcome</th>
          <th style="width: 50%;">Demonstrated Skill</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><span data-field="outcome_1">{{ outcome_1 }}</span></td>
          <td><span data-field="skill_1">{{ skill_1 }}</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span data-field="outcome_2">{{ outcome_2 }}</span></td>
          <td><span data-field="skill_2">{{ skill_2 }}</span></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span data-field="outcome_3">{{ outcome_3 }}</span></td>
          <td><span data-field="skill_3">{{ skill_3 }}</span></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">Program viability would be assessed using direct and indirect measures. Direct outcomes may describe goals for the program, such as student success metrics as defined as graduation rates, persistence factors, and transfer rates. Other methods that would provide useful feedback for improving processes that support the learning and provide an overall picture of success would include course evaluations and course grades.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 11pt;">The development of the assessment plan for the General Studies Transfer – Associate of Arts and Associate of Science partnership will include faculty and dean representation from Lakeshore Technical College and faculty and administrator representation from University of Wisconsin Oshkosh. One criterion for evaluating the success of this partnership will be the rate of student completion for bachelor's degree.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="footer">
    Paul Carlsen, Ph.D., President | gotoltc.edu | 1290 North Avenue, Cleveland, WI 53015 | 1.888.GO TO LTC | HLC Accredited hlcommission.org
  </div>
</div>